@* The shape of BitNavPanel as the Bit.BlazorUI demo configures it: a search box over grouped
   links, reproduced in plain markup because this site takes no dependency on Bit.BlazorUI.

   Clicking any link also closes the mobile drawer; on desktop the class toggle is a no-op.
   Wired via data-demo-action (see the delegated listener in demo.js) - no inline onclick, so
   the site works under a strict Content-Security-Policy.

   Each link sits in a .nav-item wrapper because the search filter in demo.js hides entries by
   toggling a class on them: the wrapper's class is rendered once and never re-rendered, while
   a class written straight onto a NavLink would be overwritten the next time NavLink
   recomputes its own active state. *@
